    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n#   Datasets:⟨3⟩\n* * *\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/69e01086cd39efcd1c558834/ZhQjxp4jzFfAjcyCUGM0i.png) ⟨28⟩\nAIIT-Threshold⟨28⟩\n/\nAIIT-Tessera24B-dataset⟨29⟩\nlike 1\nLanguages:  English ⟨30⟩ Japanese ⟨31⟩\nTags:  pretraining ⟨32⟩ curated ⟨33⟩ tessera ⟨34⟩\nLicense:\nother\n Dataset card ⟨29⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨35⟩ Community ⟨36⟩\nDataset Viewer\nThe dataset viewer is not available because its heuristics could not detect any supported data files⟨37⟩. You can try uploading⟨38⟩ some data files, or configuring⟨39⟩ the data files location manually.\n  * Contents⟨40⟩\n  * Sources⟨41⟩\n  * Data policy & honesty notes⟨42⟩\n  * ⚠️ Redistribution — read before download⟨43⟩\n  * License⟨44⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨45⟩ AIIT-Tessera24B-dataset \nThe ~24.5B-token pretraining corpus used to train Tessera 1B⟨46⟩, from AIIT-THRESHOLD.\n**What makes it different:** this is not a single lab dump. The bulk is web text (DCLM), but the long tail was **hand-selected, source by source** — a deliberate curation rather than a firehose.\n##   ⟨40⟩ Contents   \n|   |   |  \n| --- | --- |  \n| Tokens  | 24,504,827,904 seen (~24.5B); curated set ≈24.66B  |  \n| Shards  | 674, tokenized with the Tessera tokenizer⟨47⟩ (byte-level BPE, vocab 65,536, memory-organ atoms)  |  \n| Format  | uint16 token id streams (`.u16.bin`) + tokenizer + shard manifest (sha256)  |  \n| Languages  | English (primary), Japanese  |  \n##   ⟨41⟩ Sources \n**Bulk:** DCLM (web). **Hand-selected long tail:** Wikipedia, Project Gutenberg, arXiv, PubMed Open Access, USPTO patents, mC4-ja, SlimPajama, RefinedWeb, The Pile, Dolmino, HackerNews, newspapers, philosophy texts, sacred texts, NSF award abstracts, OSF, CrossRef open-access abstracts, DOAJ, GitHub issues, Magicoder-OSS-Instruct, Cosmopedia-v2, Kyoto-school texts.\n##   ⟨42⟩ Data policy & honesty notes \n  * **No model-conversation transcripts. No synthetic reasoning traces.** (Per AIIT's training-data policy⟨48⟩.)\n  * **Two components are third-party synthetic:** Cosmopedia-v2 (Mixtral-generated) and Magicoder-OSS-Instruct. Disclosed, small, public datasets — not our own model outputs.\n  * **Deduplication is exact-match only.** Fuzzy/near-dedup (MinHash) did not complete; expect some near-duplicate content.\n\n\n##   ⟨43⟩ ⚠️ Redistribution — read before download \nThis corpus is derived from many upstream datasets with **different, sometimes restrictive, licenses**. AIIT does not hold redistribution rights to all of them. Therefore this release is structured in two tiers:\n  1. **Tokens published directly** — shards from clearly redistributable sources (e.g. Wikipedia CC-BY-SA, Project Gutenberg public domain, arXiv, PubMed OA, USPTO patents, NSF/OSF/CrossRef/DOAJ open access, and permissively-licensed web).\n  2. **Recipe only (not the tokens)** — for sources whose licenses do not permit redistribution (e.g. The Pile subsets, OpenSubtitles, copyrighted newspapers). For these we publish the exact source list, filters, and tokenizer so you can **reproduce** those shards from the public originals yourself.\n\n\nThis keeps the release genuinely open without stepping on upstream terms. Every shard's tier is marked in `MANIFEST.md`.\n##   ⟨44⟩ License \nPer-source (see `SOURCES.md`). AIIT's own curation metadata, manifest, and the `tessera_tokenizer.json` are released **Apache-2.0**.\nCopy to bucket new \n\nDownloads last month\n    557\nTotal file size: 49.6 GB\n##  Models trained or fine-tuned on AIIT-Threshold/AIIT-Tessera24B-dataset\n ![](https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/69e01086cd39efcd1c558834/ZhQjxp4jzFfAjcyCUGM0i.png) AIIT-Threshold/Tessera-1B 1B • Updated 19 days ago • 838 • 5 ⟨46⟩\n##  Collection including AIIT-Threshold/AIIT-Tessera24B-dataset\n#### Human-Authored Training Data Collection No synthetic text, no model-transcript training. Every example here was written by a person. • 2 items • Updated 20 days ago ⟨49⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨50⟩ Privacy⟨51⟩ About⟨52⟩ Careers⟨53⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\n",
